<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For each $\alpha \in A$, choose a (small) set $S(\alpha )$ of morphisms of $\calC $ such that $\calC _{\alpha }$ is the full subcategory of $\calC $ spanned by the $S(\alpha )$-local objects. Then $\bigcap _{\alpha \in A} \calC _{\alpha }$ is the full subcategory of $\calC $ spanned by the $\bigcup _{\alpha \in A} S(\alpha )$-local objects. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>